  "answer": "### Short Answer\n\n### Interpretation\nFiling your income tax return after the deadline is allowed, but it will incur penalties as stipulated in the NIRC. The penalties may include a surcharge for late payment and interest on the unpaid tax. It is advisable to file as soon as possible to minimize these penalties.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIf you have missed the deadline, you should prepare and submit your income tax return promptly to avoid further penalties. Additionally, be prepared to pay any taxes due along with the applicable penalties to ensure compliance with tax regulations.",
